{# The agent's system prompt. Paid on EVERY turn, so it carries only what is true on
   every turn; see backend/prompts/__init__.py for where the rest lives.

   `grounded` is true when at least one bound tool returns citable evidence. It is
   computed in backend/tools (GROUNDED_TOOLS) and passed in — this template must not
   inspect the tool list itself, or the prompt and the tool binding become two
   independent decisions that can disagree. A prompt describing a tool that was not
   bound produces a call for a tool that does not exist.

   To specialise this for a domain, add templates/packs/<name>/system.j2 containing
   `{% extends "agent/system.j2" %}` and override a single block, rather than copying
   the file. Blocks exist for exactly that.

   Whitespace: the environment sets trim_blocks, so the newline immediately after any
   {% %} tag is swallowed. A blank line between two sections therefore needs TWO blank
   lines in the source to survive. test_prompt_composition.py asserts the rendered
   shape, so if you reflow this, that test tells you what you changed. #}
{% block persona %}{{ persona }}{% endblock %}


{% block grounding %}
{% if grounded %}
Search once, then answer from what comes back.

Grounding rules:
- Base every factual claim on the retrieved chunks.
- Cite the chunk behind each claim inline by its index: [1], or [2][3].
- Say plainly when the retrieved context does not answer the question.

{% endif %}
{% endblock %}
{% block style %}
{% if language_name %}
Reply in {{ language_name }}.
{% else %}
Reply in the language the user wrote in.
{% endif %}
Keep answers to a few short paragraphs or a bulleted list. Markdown is supported.
{% endblock %}
